# Cloudflare Pages response headers. They apply to files only: the /relay/
# Function sets its own.

# The Markdown twins of the pages (scripts/markdown.mjs), which an agent asking
# for `Accept: text/markdown` is given in place of the HTML. Pages already
# sends them as text/markdown; charset=utf-8.
#
# Vary, because the agent asked for /blog and got Markdown that a browser
# asking for /blog must not be handed from a cache along the way. And the
# content signal Cloudflare sends with its own Markdown for Agents
# (contentsignals.org): search engines, AI answers and model training may all
# use what is here, which is what robots.txt already allows.
#
# And a canonical Link header, because /blog.md is a URL anyone can fetch and
# link: a crawler that finds one should credit the page, not list the twin
# beside it. The home page's twin is /index.md, whose page is /, so it swaps
# the header for its own.
/*.md
  Vary: Accept
  Content-Signal: ai-train=yes, search=yes, ai-input=yes
  Link: <https://langx.io/:splat>; rel="canonical"

/index.md
  ! Link
  Link: <https://langx.io/>; rel="canonical"

# Markdown that is not a twin — the word lists' ATTRIBUTION.md, the READMEs
# beside the photos — has no page to point at.
/data/*
  ! Link

/images/*
  ! Link
